# Program to calculate total gadgets produced through a given day

Step 1: Analyse the provided graph and break into sections
Step 2: create variables for the 4 important points given
Step 3: build linear interpolation  keeping into account the different behaviour of the graph through different sections
Step 4: run the code  to determine a relationship
Step 5: test for inconsistancies and  plug in test values
Step 6: Submit to gradescope

variables:
Point_A: coordinates of point A
Point_B: coordinates of point B
Point_C: coordinates of point C
Point_D: coordinates of point D
Point_E: coordinates of point E
Result:  give the  value of heat flux
x1:      random input value from the user
Slope:   holds the slope of linear interpolation

Test Cases:

Normal Cases:
Test 1 at delta 1<TE<5 output should lie between: (10^3,10^4)
Test 2 at delta 5<TE<30 output should lie between: (10^4,10^6)
Test 3 at delta 30<TE<120 output should lie between: (10^4,10^6)
Test 4 at delta 120<TE<1000 output should lie between: (10^4,10^7)
Test 5 at delta TE = 2 output should lie between: (10^3,10^4)
Test 6 at delta TE = 15 output should lie between: (10^4,10^6)
Test 7 at delta TE = 60 output should lie between: (10^4,10^6)
Test 8 at delta TE = 500 output should lie between: (10^4,10^7)

Edge Cases:
Test 9 at delta TE<1 output<0
Test 10 at delta 1000<TE 10^7<output


